Sure! Here’s a quick example of how you can pull Apple’s most recent annual income statement using the `requests_get` function:

```json
{
  "name": "requests_get",
  "arguments": {
    "url": "https://financialmodelingprep.com/api/v3/income-statement",
    "params": {
      "symbol": "AAPL",
      "period": "annual",
      "datatype": "json",
      "limit": 1
    },
    "apikey": "YOUR_API_KEY"
  }
}
```

Replace `"YOUR_API_KEY"` with your actual FMP API key. This will return the latest annual income statement for Apple in JSON format. If you’d like to fetch quarterly data, change `"period"` to `"quarter"`, or adjust `"limit"` to retrieve more years. Let me know if you’d like help tailoring the request further!
